By considering,  $b_i=a_i^n$ , inequality is equivalent to showing,  $$ b_1-b_2+b_3-\cdots+b_{2n+1}<\sqrt[n]{b_1^n-b_2^n+\cdots+b_{2n+1}^n}. $$  By induction on  $n$ , we will prove that, for every  $n$ , and every positive reals  $b_1<b_2<\cdots<b_{2n+1}$ , and every positive integer  $m$ , it holds that,  $$ b_1-b_2+b_3-\cdots+b_{2n+1}<\sqrt[n]{b_1^m-b_2^m+\cdots+b_{2n+1}^m}. $$  Let us begin with the base case,  $n=1$ . Our goal is to prove,  $(b_1-b_2+b_3)^m<b_1^m-b_2^m+b_3^m$ . Note that, this is equivalent to proving,  $$ (b_3-b_2)\left(
\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}b_3^i b_2^{m-1-i}\right)\geq (b_3-b_2)\left(\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}(b_3-b_2+b_1)^i b_1^{m-1-i}\right), $$  which is obvious, since  $b_3>b_3-b_2+b_1>0$  and  $b_3>b_2>b_1$ .

We now execute the inductive hypothesis. Suppose the statement is true for every integer up to and including  $n-1$ . Now, take  $a_1<a_2<\cdots<a_{2n+1}$ . Notice that with  $\widehat{a}_{2n-1}=a_{2n+1}-a_{2n}+a_{2n-1}$ ,
\begin{align*}
a_1-a_2+\cdots+a_{2n+1}&=a_1-a_2+\cdots-a_{2n-2}+\widehat{a}_{2n-1} 
&\leq \sqrt[m]{a_1^m-a_2^m+\cdots-a_{2n-2}^m+\widehat{a}_{2n-1}^m}.
\end{align*}
The goal is therefore, to show that,  $$ \widehat{a}_{2n-1}^m = (a_{2n+1}-a_{2n}+a_{2n-1})^m\leq a_{2n-1}^m-a_{2n}^m+a_{2n+1}^m, $$  which is nothing but the the hypothesis for  $n=1$ . Hence, the proof is complete.

