The main idea is to compute the ratio  $\frac{AT}{TB}$  with the help of the **Ratio Lemma** in  $\triangle AQB$ . 
\begin{align*}
\frac{AT}{TB} &= \frac{QA \sin \theta}{QB \cos \theta} 
 &= \frac{QA}{QB} \tan \theta 
&= \tan \beta \tan \theta,
\end{align*}
where the last line comes from  $\triangle AQB$ . Finally, we will compute  $\tan \alpha$  and  $\tan \beta$  from  $\triangle XAB$  and  $\triangle YAB$ . This yields 
\[ \frac{AT}{TB} = \tan \alpha \tan \beta = \frac{AX}{2} \times \frac{AY}{2} = \frac{|AX| \cdot |AY|}{4} = \frac{k}{4}\]
which is a constant. Since  $AT + TB = 2$  is fixed as well, we get that  $T$  is fixed as desired.  $\blacksquare$

